# Build output. The source is build.mjs, style.css and lang.js; public/ is
# generated from them on every build, locally and on Vercel. Committing it
# guarantees the committed HTML drifts from the source that produced it, and
# the drift stays invisible until someone reads the wrong copy.
public/

# THIS RULE LIVES HERE, NOT IN THE ROOT .gitignore, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.
# The root .gitignore is an input to the Expo fingerprint (it shows up as a
# `bareGitIgnore` source in `expo-updates fingerprint:generate`). Editing it
# changes runtimeVersion, which orphans every build already in the field from
# any future OTA update. Nested .gitignore files are not fingerprint sources.
# Put project-local ignores in the subdirectory that owns them.
